    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="1093" n="993" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg993"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.42157 Detroit/89</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Canada</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robbins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 829</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-10-06">October 6,
                        1934</date>.<lb/>[Received October 8.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Legation’s despatches No. 734 of March 24, 1932,<anchor n="98" xml:id="d742-f1"
                    /> and No. 518 of April 11, 1934, relative to the dredging operations being
                    carried on in the channel of the lower Detroit River, and to transmit herewith
                    copies of a further note from the Acting Secretary of State for External Affairs
                    on this subject.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren D. Robbins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d742-a1.xml" xpointer="d742-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
